WEBVTT

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.560
Whoa! This ain't good!

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.230
Wake up, Neku!

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.440
Scramble Crossing.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.320
Another day went by?

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.610
How can you act so laid-back?!

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.580
We've only got three days left,
including today!

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.160
We've gotta get Rhyme back from Ironface

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.920
and beat the Composer
at the Shibuya River, too!

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.540
Calm down a little.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.960
How am I supposed to calm down?!

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.170
We've got to work in order.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:57.140
Let's check everywhere we can go
with the keypin we got yesterday.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.430
Umm... I'm pretty sure...

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.350
...he said it'd get us into anywhere
an officer's would, right?

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.270
What a wonderful world such would be.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.080
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:44.990
"#10: The Countless Wrongs of Our Day"

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.450
"#10: The Countless Wrongs of Our Day"
What's going on?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.000
To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.960
...we shine this light
of true redemption...

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.300
This creeps me out.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.550
They're all thinking the same thing.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.010
Shibuya is...

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.850
...that this place may become as paradise.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.140
What a wonderful world such would be.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.020
Shibuya is supposed to be
full of all kinds of people

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.480
thinking and doing different things.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.240
To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.610
...we shine this light
of true redemption...

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.160
--I didn't want to collide with people,
so I covered my ears.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.660
--...that this place may
become as paradise.
--I didn't want to collide with people,
so I covered my ears.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.200
What a wonderful world such would be.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.410
But now, I can tell.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:30.870
--To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.750
--This place...
--To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.250
...we shine this light
of true redemption...

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.050
...that this place may become as paradise.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.220
What a wonderful world such would be.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.850
I knew it! It's gotta be
those Red Skull pins!

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.680
The Composer...

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.890
...is CAT!

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.270
It's the exact same design!

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:56.150
However you figure it,
CAT's gotta be pullin' the strings!

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.520
There's no way.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.440
How can you be so sure?

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.780
CAT is really Mr. Hanekoma.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.280
Huh? You mean <i>that </i>Hanekoma?

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.000
The one who saved me and Rhyme?

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.540
Yeah.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.500
Huh? Uh...

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.000
Why's everything gotta be so complicated?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.590
You're sure? Honest?

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.800
I'm positive. Joshua told me.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.350
Joshua was looking for the Composer too.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.680
Mr. Hanekoma was helping him do it.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.440
So, Mr. Hanekoma,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.480
CAT,

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.360
isn't the Composer!

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.740
Mr. Hanekoma taught me
to expand my horizons.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:46.320
He said it was so I could enjoy life.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.830
To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.250
...we shine this light
of true redemption...

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.210
...that this place may become as paradise.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.420
--A Shibuya like this...
--What a wonderful world such would be.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.920
...isn't Shibuya at all.
--What a wonderful world such would be.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.760
If you wanna trust him that badly...

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:10.510
So, uh, where haven't we gone
lookin' for Ironface yet?

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.600
Let's think.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.600
We've already been to...

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:15.940
...Hachiko,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.310
the underpass,

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:18.770
Ten-Four,

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.400
Dogenzaka,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.360
O-East,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.740
Miyashita Park,

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.530
Tower Records,

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.030
Marui,

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.450
Parco,

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.120
Tokyu Hands,

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.080
and Tipsy Tose Hall.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:39.290
So, we still haven't been
to Cat Street or AMX.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.340
OK, let's keep lookin'!

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.010
Udagawa too.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.300
"AMX"

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.090
Wait.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.640
There're Reapers around.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.640
Hey, do they seem weird to you?

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:59.560
To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.360
Yo, Reaper's too? For real?

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:05.900
...that this place may become as paradise.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.990
What a wonderful world such would be.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:12.830
Here they come! Stay focused!

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.540
I'll finish this in no time flat!

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.560
What a wonderful world such would...

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.390
Even the Reapers are acting weird.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.600
What's happening to the
Underground and Realground?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.730
Damn it.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:45.400
You never hold back, huh?

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:50.490
Only lately. I used to be the opposite.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.990
<i>You</i>?

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:57.250
I didn't have anything
I could lose myself in.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:01.920
But my folks got their hopes up
anyway and got let down.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:06.300
Still, Rhyme was always there for me.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.050
She said I'd find my dream.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:15.010
That bein' alive means making
your future--your dreams--yourself.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:19.310
So, I found my dream:
to be the world's best skater.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.770
I'm gonna win this game
and change the world!

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:32.530
I'll bring back Rhyme, and Shiki,
and everybody else the Reapers killed!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.240
That's my dream now!

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.450
What's that?

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:40.710
The walls!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.290
Ever seen 'em do that?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.500
Never.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:51.590
That took longer than I calculated.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:56.680
I zetta can't get the hang of this body.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.350
Oh well. I'll adjust eventually.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:08.190
Time to resume my calculations.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.530
The wall is broken?

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.450
Somethin' got it from inside, like, <i>boom</i>!

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.790
It looks like it forced its way out.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.960
Could anyone actually pull this off?

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:27.590
Something happened. That's for sure.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:28.920
Who cares?!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:32.760
"Nothing ventured, nothing--
whatever they say!"

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.550
Try to care a <i>little</i>!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:36.850
"Udagawa"

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:38.140
"Udagawa"
Whoa.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.890
What happened here?

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.310
Yo, check that out.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.280
This is... the weird design
Minamimoto was drawing.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:02.120
So, Ironface ain't here?

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.370
This ain't the time for snapshots!

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.790
I'm taking photos of the past
to find out what happened.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.550
Man, how dumb can you be?!

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.510
Everyone knows that's impossible!

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.050
I can take them.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.880
I don't have time to explain.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.890
Wh-What the...?

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:24.310
What's it show?

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:27.650
I-It's Hanekoma!

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.310
Mr. Hanekoma.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:33.570
Yo, hang on, don't tell me
<i>he </i>drew this thing?!

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.200
What the hell did he conjure up?!

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.370
To right the countless
wrongs of our day...

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.290
Huh?

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.120
No way.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.460
We shine...

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.040
Not you too!

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.300
...this light of true redemption...

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.150
Shit!

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.770
These guys are crazy tough!

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.620
They aren't...

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.280
...even trying...

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:22.780
...to dodge our attacks!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:36.340
Hey! Wake the hell up!

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.330
Smash his glowing pin!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.170
--What?!
--Just let 'im have it!

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.250
Focus!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.460
Fine.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.490
Looks like... they stopped.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.320
They're nothing like yesterday.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:50.330
I bet these things are
what made 'em go nuts.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:54.540
Why are Reapers wearing Red Skull pins?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.630
The ones the Reapers have are
supposed to be called "O-Pins."

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:04.600
There's no mistake. They're all the
same design by CAT--Mr. Hanekoma.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.680
Beat, I'm going to Mr. Hanekoma's café,

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:14.100
and I'm gonna make him tell me
everything he knows about Shibuya.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.940
"Cat Street"

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:23.860
Whoa. This wall's busted up too.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.370
Did something go to Cat Street?

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.910
This area still seems normal.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.040
Let's hurry!

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.380
--What the...?
--Whoa!

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:52.560
Someone trashed this place.
Think it was the old dude?

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.560
No way.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:57.900
Why would he wreck his own café?

00:12:57.900 --> 00:12:59.530
I guess you're right.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:05.570
There's no one left here.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:10.330
Whoever destroyed the wall
probably came after Mr. Hanekoma.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:13.960
Maybe Ironface? Do you think
she pulled a hit and run?

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.130
I'm not sure.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.880
Oh, let's take a bunch
of those special photos!

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.090
One of 'em's gotta show something.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.970
I can only take one more.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:31.470
He said it drains so much battery
that I can only take two per day.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.400
It's Mr. Hanekoma!

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.530
Looks like he hid somethin'.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:45.820
Let's look.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.030
Yeah.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.580
An envelope?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.830
There's somethin' in it.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.510
A keypin?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.800
Isn't that a Reaper keypin?

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:10.430
No, I've never seen one like this before.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:13.270
I know this design from somewhere.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:18.440
Talk about creepy.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.900
It's in here.

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:24.570
We checked it out.
You'd better be satisfied.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.400
Either way, it appears there's a wall.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.490
Sure it's not just dark?

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:32.240
It's a bit different from
the others we've seen.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.750
Did you remember where?

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.710
The Shibuya River.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:43.590
Does that mean he's
tellin' us to go there?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.010
There's something else.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.220
A letter?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:57.390
"There's just one simple trick
to survive in this Shibuya:

00:14:57.390 --> 00:15:00.850
No matter what, enjoy every
moment with all you've got.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:05.940
Watch out for shadows and
find out where Konishi really is.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:09.450
That's when the real battle will begin."

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.910
All right! This settles it!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.790
Ironface has gotta be
at the Shibuya River!

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.120
Why?

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.250
Huh?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:25.170
Why does Mr. Hanekoma have a
keypin to get into the Shibuya River?

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:28.300
Joshua wanted to get back there.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:30.880
Mr. Hanekoma must have known that.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.850
So, why'd he leave that keypin for me?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:40.640
What are you trying to make
me do, Mr. Hanekoma?

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.360
We ain't got time to waste wonderin'!

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:50.110
We'll take Rhyme back from Ironface,
then take the fight to the Composer!

00:15:55.910 --> 00:16:00.290
Hey! Who left this
big pile of trash here?!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.870
This junk is...

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.420
So, you're still alive,

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.470
you hectopascals!

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.680
H-He's...!

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:19.180
I calculated all this out!

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.480
Minamimoto?! Weren't you erased?!

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:27.440
...is my answer!

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:31.570
This was always the point of that move.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:34.740
I used the Taboo Psych
"Resurrection" to erase myself

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:38.120
and then come back from a Refinery!

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:40.580
So, that was <i>you </i>in Udagawa!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.540
Zetta duh!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:51.260
Check it out. This is my
latest masterpiece:

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.800
Myself!

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.010
Your body...

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:59.390
I turned it Taboo.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:04.310
This power will let me go
toe-to-toe with the Composer.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.940
No way.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.530
Convention is just trash!

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.530
Crush!

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.660
On the scrap heap it goes!

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:22.040
Only my aesthetics have value.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.460
The next Composer is gonna be me!

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.170
Why did you kill me?!

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:31.050
Are you behind all these
changes in Shibuya?!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:34.090
When Kitaniji made the O-Pins mandatory,

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:38.260
the Underground was
already starting to change.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:43.100
That means the Composer is responsible
for the changes in Shibuya!

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:46.770
You know where Hanekoma is, don't you?

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.020
As if!

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:54.780
This Taboo conversion
of his is worthy of me.

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:58.740
Mr. Hanekoma is the one
who turned him Taboo?

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.580
What for?

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:04.080
Where is he? Where'd he run off to?

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:06.000
I know you know!

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.210
You know where he is!

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:10.380
You're the one who trashed Wildkat!

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:17.300
Zetta duh!

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:24.560
I'll use you for a warmup.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.270
Attention, zeroes!

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:30.610
You get to die 4 my cause!

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:32.320
Let's go all-out.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:33.570
Yeah!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:56.760
Slabs of Ham, Celery And Horseradish,
Tons Of Asparagus!

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:02.970
Beat!

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:09.770
What?!

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:26.160
This guy's for real.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.370
You don't stand a chance.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:37.300
I'll be the one to rule this world!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:39.300
Zetta Crush!

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.640
I'm all warmed up now.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:52.440
That's enough calibration.

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:58.320
This time, Composer, you're mine.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:11.420
What?!

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.040
Scramble Crossing?!

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.460
That means...

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.050
...we're on day six!

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:24.340
I bet he headed to the Shibuya River.

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:25.890
Then we've gotta move!

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:32.560
We've got the Shibuya River key.
He can't get ahead of us.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:38.230
He said he should be on par
with the Composer now, right?

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:40.280
Yeah, so?

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:44.820
So, the Composer's as strong as he is.
Maybe stronger.

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:49.700
Rhyme...

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.410
Rhyme is waiting!

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.710
I'm going.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:58.300
I'm gonna go, go, go, go, go, go!

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:02.930
Seriously?

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:10.390
Shibuya River. The Composer. Mr. Hanekoma.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.250
